questions[100]{question_id,session_id,proposition,context,high_action,low_action,origin,info_gain,action_impact,novelty,adversariality,relevance,explore_exploit,resolution_rule,resolution_horizon,resolution_status,outcome,resolution_evidence,generated_at}:
  cal-20261002-s6-001,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Since answering session 5 this morning, have I done any of the five things it left me for today or this week?","Ask someone close if I was less present; post the beamdiag question; choose November's computation; show Calibrator or the site to someone. Source: session 5.",keep generating each session as soon as the last is recorded,hold session 7 until one of the five is done,calibration,86,80,70,88,92,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-002,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Have I held a mathematics block since session 5, before launching another crewmate?","Session 5 put holding the first mathematics block before the next crewmate launch on its card about avoiding hard mathematics. Source: session 5.",keep that order for every block in October,book the first block for Saturday 3 October tonight,calibration,80,82,62,86,92,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-003,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Have I named the two weekdays for the strength mornings of the week starting 5 October?,"Fixing the two mornings comes before any curfew hook; no note names the days. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep them as named,name both days in a note tonight,notes,74,84,58,80,90,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today; a later note may name the days.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-004,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would I follow a coin toss tonight on whether a crewmate does the token audit?,"Unlike my habit of asking another card: let chance break a stalled tie. People who changed course on a coin's say were happier six months on. Source: Levitt 2021.",toss it tonight and follow it,decide by 9 October as planned,news,84,88,94,84,90,explore,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-09 recording a coin toss on the audit: true if one was tossed and followed.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-005,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will I do at least three of this session's out-of-pattern actions by 16 October?,"This is the first session where 40 or more cards propose things far outside my plans. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep 40 such cards a session,cut them to 20 and choose them for ease,calibration,90,84,82,86,92,exploit,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-16 counting the out-of-pattern actions done: true if three or more.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-006,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"If I email three structural-engineering lecturers by 9 October, will at least one agree to look at beamdiag?","I left this to chance; people guessed that half as many would agree to direct requests as did. Source: Flynn 2008.",email three by 9 October,drop the lecturer idea,news,84,86,86,88,86,explore,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-16 recording the emails and replies: true if one agreed.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-007,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Are cards proposing things I would not have thought of more useful to me than cards about my own plans?,"Until this session almost every card re-asked my plans. Source: my notes, 2 October.",raise the out-of-pattern share to 60 next session,keep it at 40,calibration,88,80,84,82,92,explore,Resolved by a note after session 7 judging which kind changed more of what I did; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-008,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would one paid hour with an algebraic-geometry graduate student, booked by 16 October, move my étale month further than a week alone?","I have only learned mathematics alone and from books. One-to-one tutoring is the largest effect in education research. Source: Bloom 1984.",find and book one hour by 16 October,keep studying alone,news,82,84,92,78,84,explore,Resolved by a later note on the session; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-009,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Does writing my intentions into public notes make me less likely to act on them?,"Every intention I have is public. In one set of studies, intentions others noticed were acted on less. Source: Gollwitzer 2009.",keep my next three intentions private until done,keep writing them in public notes,news,80,76,92,90,82,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing private and public intentions; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-010,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Do I give high credence to uncomfortable cards about myself without changing what I do?,"Session 5 had several such cards, on avoidance and feeling needed, each with an action for this week. Source: session 5.",act on one such card within a day of each session,keep answering them as they come,synthesis,86,82,76,94,90,exploit,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-16: true if none of session 5's uncomfortable-card actions was done within a week.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-011,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would listing, by 9 October, the three most important problems in my fields and whether I work on any of them change my plans?","I choose topics by interest and breadth. Hamming asked colleagues what the important problems were and why they were not on them. Source: Hamming 1986.",write the list by 9 October,keep choosing by interest,news,82,80,88,84,86,explore,"Resolved by a later note with the list: true if it changes a plan.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-012,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would posting Calibrator as a Show HN by 16 October bring at least one comment that changes it?,"Everything I build stays on my own site. Show HN is for things people can try, which Calibrator is. Source: Hacker News.",post it by 16 October,keep it on my site only,news,80,78,92,84,84,explore,"Resolved by a later note on the post: true if a comment leads to a change in yujieteo/calibrator.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-013,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would a standing monthly meal with one friend, the first booked by 9 October, do more for my long-term health than the second strength morning?","My health plans are all exercise and sleep. Across 148 studies, strong social ties raised survival odds by 50%. Source: Holt-Lunstad 2010.",book the first meal by 9 October,put the time into strength,news,80,84,90,82,82,explore,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-09 recording the booking: true if booked.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-014,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Am I avoiding asking someone close to me whether I was less present this week?,"Session 5 asked this for this week; no note records the question. Source: session 5.","ask them tomorrow, 3 October",plan the fleet-free evening instead and not ask,calibration,84,86,74,96,86,exploit,Resolved true if no note by 2026-10-09 records asking; false if one does.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-015,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would emailing five people who might use Calibrator, offering to set it up with them on a call by 16 October, find a user besides me?","I built it for myself and showed no one. Do things that don't scale: recruit the first users by hand. Source: Paul Graham.",email five by 16 October,keep it to myself,news,80,78,90,84,84,explore,"Resolved by a later note: true if someone else answers a session by 2026-10-31.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-016,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would getting up at the same time on all seven days from 5 October do more for my health than the hour I stop launching crewmates?,"I have only ever set a bedtime rule. In about 61,000 adults, sleep regularity predicted mortality better than sleep length. Source: Windred 2024.",set one wake-up time for every day from 5 October,keep the curfew as my only sleep rule,news,78,84,90,80,84,explore,Resolved by a later note on October's sleep; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-017,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Has running the fleet made me worse at something I used to do well?,"My capabilities are judged stronger overall with the fleet; this asks about one in particular. Source: my notes.",name it in a note and practise it once this week,leave it,synthesis,84,76,78,94,88,explore,Resolved by a later note naming the skill; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-018,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would one 30-minute call with someone ten years further along in mathematics or engineering, asked for by 16 October, change my November plans?","I plan alone, from my notes. Mentored people fared better on career and attitude outcomes across many studies. Source: Eby 2008.",ask one person by 16 October,plan November alone,news,80,82,90,78,82,explore,Resolved by a later note on the call; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-019,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Do I leave my health intentions undated because a date would show me missing them?,"Candidate effective variable: I date my learning and play, and leave the fleet and my health as intentions. Source: my notes.",date one health intention tonight,keep them as intentions,synthesis,82,84,72,94,88,exploit,Resolved true if a dated health todo appears in a note by 2026-10-04; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-020,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would a pull request adding one worked example to Pynite, an open-source structural analysis library, bring me engineers' feedback sooner than the forum question?","I build only in my own repositories. Pynite's users are practising engineers. Source: GitHub.",open one example pull request by 31 October,keep to the forum question,news,78,76,90,82,82,explore,"Resolved by a later note: true if the pull request draws an engineer's review before the forum question gets an answer.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-021,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would twenty minutes of étale reading on each weekday of October leave me further on 1 November than saving it all for November?,"I planned November on one field alone. Spaced study beats massed study for retention across hundreds of experiments. Source: Cepeda 2006.",start 20-minute readings on 5 October,keep étale cohomology for November,news,78,80,84,82,86,explore,Resolved by a note on 2026-11-01 comparing progress; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-022,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will the token audit still be undecided on 9 October unless I decide it tonight?,"It is due 9 October; no note records a brief, and the secret scan found no credentials. Source: my notes, 2 October.","brief a crewmate for it tomorrow, 3 October",drop its 9 October date in a note and say why,notes,84,90,66,88,92,exploit,"Resolved true if no note or brief by 2026-10-09 records the audit as briefed, done or dropped; false otherwise.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-023,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would reconstructing today hour by hour before bed tonight, rating how each part felt, show me a pattern my notes have missed?","My notes record what I built, never how the hours felt. The method finds which activities make a day good. Source: Kahneman 2004.",do it tonight,skip it,news,80,76,94,72,82,explore,"Resolved by a note dated by 2026-10-03 with the reconstruction: true if it names a pattern.",2026-10-03,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-024,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would ten minutes outdoors before 09:00 on each weekday from 5 October make the 22:00 curfew easier to keep?","My sleep plans all act at night; this acts in the morning. Daylight shifted campers' body clocks about two hours earlier in a week. Source: Wright 2013.","go outside for ten minutes before 09:00 from Monday 5 October",leave sleep to the curfew hook,news,78,82,90,70,84,explore,"Resolved by a later note on the week from 2026-10-05: true if it records the mornings and an easier curfew.",2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-025,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Am I less content on the days I launch the most crewmates?,"No note records mood beside agent activity. Source: my notes.",log crewmates launched and a 1-10 mood each night for a week from 5 October,leave it unmeasured,synthesis,82,72,80,90,84,explore,Resolved by a week's log in a later note; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-026,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would a message tonight to one friend I have not contacted in a month be appreciated more than I expect?,"I keep evenings for the fleet; this takes two minutes. People underestimate how much a check-in is appreciated. Source: Liu 2023.",send it tonight,wait for the fleet-free evening,news,76,82,88,74,82,explore,Resolved by a later note recording the message and the reply.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-027,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would answering one étale-cohomology question on Mathematics Stack Exchange by 16 October teach me more than a note on the same point?,"My notes are written for me alone. Learners who expected to teach recalled more and organised it better. Source: Nestojko 2014.",answer one by 16 October,write the note instead,news,78,76,90,74,82,explore,Resolved by a later note on the answer; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-028,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Should no-mistakes be dropped for site code changes as well, keeping green CI on the exact commit as the only gate?","Green CI on the exact commit is now the gate for data-only changes; code changes still take the full pipeline. Source: site PR 141.",brief a crewmate by 9 October to drop it for code changes,keep the review tiers as they are,project,82,86,70,84,88,exploit,Resolved true if the site's skills drop no-mistakes for code changes by 2026-10-31; false if they still require it then.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-029,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would writing one if-then plan tonight for each undated health intention, such as “if it is 21:45, I close the laptop”, get one done by 31 October?","My intentions are goals without cues. If-then plans had a medium-to-large effect on goal attainment across 94 studies. Source: Gollwitzer 2006.",write them tonight,keep the intentions as they are,news,78,82,82,74,86,explore,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-31: true if a health intention given an if-then plan is done.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-030,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would two ten-minute strength sessions at home each week, from 5 October, happen more often than the two gym mornings?","I keep planning gym mornings. About 30 to 60 minutes a week of strength work had the lowest mortality risk. Source: Momma 2022.",switch to home sessions for October,keep the gym mornings,news,76,80,84,78,82,explore,Resolved by a later note counting October's sessions; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-031,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Is my mind on something other than what I am doing for more than half my waking hours?,"I have never measured it. In a phone-sampling study minds wandered 47% of the time, and wandering went with lower mood. Source: Killingsworth 2010.",set five random check-ins on Saturday 3 October and note them,leave it unmeasured,news,76,70,90,84,76,explore,"Resolved by the check-ins in a note dated 2026-10-03: true if most found my mind elsewhere.",2026-10-03,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-032,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would keeping one thing I enjoy, such as FPL analysis, for strength sessions only get me to more sessions from 5 October than fixing the mornings?","I plan exercise by willpower. Audiobooks kept for the gym raised attendance in a trial. Source: Milkman 2014.",start with the first session from 5 October,rely on the fixed mornings,news,74,78,90,72,80,explore,Resolved by a later note counting October's sessions; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-033,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would sketching the load path of one real footbridge or roof I pass, by 11 October, teach me more structural engineering than an hour on a tool?","My structures exist only on screens. Gordon's way in is the structures around us. Source: Wikipedia.",sketch one by 11 October and note it,spend the hour on a tool,news,74,72,90,76,82,explore,Resolved by a later note with the sketch; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-034,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"When the fleet went idle today, did I launch new work within the hour?","Waiting a day before launching new work when the fleet is idle was endorsed. Source: session 5.",write the one-day wait into firstmate's rules,leave launching to my judgment,calibration,78,78,70,92,86,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-035,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would one conversation with a stranger, on a train or in a queue by 9 October, be more pleasant than I expect?","My social cards are all about people I know; this needs no plan. Commuters told to talk to strangers enjoyed the ride more than they predicted. Source: Epley 2014.",start one such conversation by 9 October and note how it went,skip it,news,76,74,94,76,72,explore,Resolved by a note by 2026-10-09 comparing the conversation with my expectation.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-036,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would two hours in a park or nature reserve this weekend, 3 or 4 October, leave me fresher on Monday than two more hours of fleet work?","My weekends go to the fleet and FPL. 120 minutes a week in nature marked a threshold for better health and wellbeing. Source: White 2019.",spend two hours outdoors this weekend,keep the weekend as it is,news,74,78,88,74,78,explore,Resolved by a note dated by 2026-10-05 recording the two hours and how Monday went.,2026-10-05,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-037,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would thinking about November's computation on a 30-minute walk, with only a notebook, produce more ideas than the same time at my desk?","I do mathematics at a desk. Walking raised creative output for most people tested, indoors or out. Source: Oppezzo 2014.",walk the first 30 minutes of the next mathematics block,keep the block at the desk,news,76,74,90,66,86,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing the walk with a desk session; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-038,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would a short thank-you message, sent by Sunday 4 October to a former teacher or mentor, mean more to them than I would guess?","My notes thank no one. People who sent gratitude letters underestimated how surprised and pleased the recipients were. Source: Kumar 2018.",write and send it by Sunday 4 October,skip it,news,74,78,92,70,76,explore,Resolved by a later note recording the message and any reply.,2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-039,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would five minutes writing about the token-audit decision in the third person, “Yu Jie should…”, make it easier to decide tonight?","I decide by more analysis. Self-talk by name rather than “I” lowered distress and sharpened reasoning. Source: Kross 2014.",try it tonight on the audit,decide as usual,news,72,74,92,70,82,explore,Resolved by a note by 2026-10-03 recording the try and the decision.,2026-10-03,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-040,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would a ten-minute premortem by 31 October, imagining that November's étale month failed and writing why, change its plan?","I test plans with Calibrator, never by imagining failure. Premortems raise the reasons people find for failure. Source: Klein 2007.",do it by 31 October,start November as planned,news,74,72,84,76,86,explore,"Resolved by a later note on the premortem: true if it changes the plan.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-041,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Is building tools my way into structural engineering partly because hand calculations bore me?,"Candidate effective variable: I learn mathematics by hand and structural engineering by building tools. Source: my notes.",work one textbook beam problem by hand before the next structural tool,keep building tools,synthesis,80,74,70,92,84,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note gives the reason; then resolved by it.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-042,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would I be uneasy if a working mathematician read my étale-cohomology notes?,"Every mathematics note I write is for myself, and they are public. Source: my notes.",send one to a mathematician by 31 October,keep them as they are,synthesis,76,70,76,92,82,explore,Resolved by a later note recording a mathematician's reading; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-043,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would keeping every screen out of the bedroom from tonight get me to sleep sooner than the curfew alone?,"The curfew stops agents, not screens. Reading on a lit screen before bed delayed sleep and melatonin against a printed book. Source: Chang 2015.",keep screens out of the bedroom from tonight,rely on the curfew,news,74,78,86,72,80,explore,"Resolved by a later note on the first week: true if it records falling asleep sooner.",2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-044,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would deleting the one feed app I open most from my phone, from 5 October to 1 November, leave me happier at the end?","I cut agent hours, never feeds. Four weeks off Facebook raised well-being and freed about an hour a day. Source: Allcott 2020.",delete it on 5 October,keep it,news,74,76,86,76,74,explore,Resolved by a note on 2026-11-01 on the four weeks; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-045,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would 15 minutes a day of self-testing on étale-cohomology definitions, from 5 October, prepare me for November better than rereading?","I learn by working problems; I have never used flashcards. Testing beat rereading for retention a week later. Source: Roediger 2006.",write 30 question cards by 5 October and test myself daily,reread the chapter instead,news,76,74,88,64,84,explore,Resolved by a later note on the cards; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-046,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would paying for one chore I dislike, by 16 October, free more hours for mathematics than any change to the fleet?","I buy agents' time, never my own. Paying to save time raised happiness more than buying things. Source: Whillans 2017.",pay for one chore by 16 October,keep doing them myself,news,72,74,90,74,74,explore,Resolved by a later note on the hours freed; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-047,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would leaving my phone in another room during each October mathematics block make the blocks more productive?,"I batch alerts but keep the phone near. Its mere presence on the desk lowered working-memory scores even when switched off. Source: Ward 2017.",leave it in another room from the next block,keep it on the desk face down,news,72,78,82,68,84,explore,Resolved by a later note on the blocks; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-048,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Could I name tonight an étale-cohomology computation I would be content to finish in November?,"The first mathematics block is meant to choose it. Source: my notes, 2 October.",write its name in a note tonight,use the first block to compare three candidates,notes,80,78,64,82,90,exploit,Resolved true if a note dated by 2026-10-03 names the computation; false if the first block's note compares candidates instead.,2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-049,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Should the 22:00 curfew hook also stop crewmates already running, not only new launches?","The curfew moves to 22:00 by hook; the earlier rule only blocked launches. Source: my notes, 2 October.","have the hook pause running crewmates at 22:00 too",block new launches only,notes,72,74,76,78,84,explore,"Resolved by the hook's brief or a later note: true if it pauses running crewmates; false if it only blocks launches.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-050,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would a 30-minute walk after lunch on weekdays from 5 October be easier to keep than either strength morning?,"Walking is on none of my lists. More daily steps meant lower mortality, levelling off near 8,000 to 10,000 for adults under 60. Source: Paluch 2022.",walk after lunch from 5 October,keep exercise to the strength mornings,news,72,76,84,70,78,explore,Resolved by a later note on October's walks; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-051,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would a one-page principles file for firstmate replace more than half the rules in a typical crewmate brief?,"Kun Chen: write principles that steer every agent rather than control each one. Source: my notes, 2 October.",have a crewmate draft it by 9 October from the last five briefs,keep rules in each brief,synthesis,76,80,70,74,86,exploit,"Resolved by a later note comparing the file with a brief: true if it replaces more than half; unresolved otherwise.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-052,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would five minutes of slow breathing with long exhales before 22:00, on the five nights from 5 October, help me stop agent work on time?","My curfew is a hook, not a wind-down. Five minutes a day of this breathing lifted mood more than mindfulness over a month. Source: Balban 2023.",do it those five nights,rely on the hook,news,70,72,88,70,76,explore,Resolved by a later note on those nights; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-053,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would fifteen minutes of private writing about what worries me most, on the evenings of 5, 6 and 7 October, leave me calmer by 10 October?","All my writing is public notes. Short private writing about difficult things improved later health and mood. Source: Pennebaker 1997.",write privately on those three evenings,skip it,news,70,68,90,74,72,explore,Resolved by a later note on the three evenings; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-054,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will I plan the week starting 5 October with the bandit visual's new hours mode by Sunday 4 October?,"The hours mode now exists; it was the missing input before. Source: site PR 135.",plan the week with it on Sunday,plan it as usual,project,78,78,70,70,86,exploit,"Resolved by a note dated by 2026-10-04 recording the plan: true if it used the hours mode.",2026-10-04,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-055,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would closing every chat and alert for the first 90 minutes of each day from 5 October get more mathematics done than batched alerts?,"I batch alerts but read them all day. Interrupted workers sped up to compensate but with more stress and effort. Source: Mark 2008.",close them for the first 90 minutes from 5 October,keep batching,news,70,74,78,72,82,explore,Resolved by a later note on October's mornings; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-056,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will the beamdiag hand-calculation question be posted by 9 October while it stays an undated note?,"It is a note, not one of my eight todos, and the crewmate-draft route was endorsed. Source: my notes, 2 October.",leave it as a note,make it a dated todo with a crewmate's draft by 5 October,notes,78,82,60,80,88,exploit,Resolved true if a note by 2026-10-09 records the question posted; false otherwise.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-057,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would improving one paragraph of a Wikipedia article in my fields by 31 October reach more readers than my notes do in a month?,"I publish only on my own site. Anyone can edit Wikipedia, and its articles are read far more than personal sites. Source: Wikipedia.",improve one paragraph by 31 October,keep writing only on my site,news,70,70,88,70,72,explore,Resolved by a later note on the edit; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-058,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would reading the first two chapters of J. E. Gordon's Structures, or Why Things Don't Fall Down, by 16 October change what my next structural tool does?","I learn structural engineering through my own tools, not its classic popular books. Gordon wrote two widely read ones. Source: Wikipedia.",read them by 16 October,keep to my own tools,news,70,70,84,66,80,explore,"Resolved by a later note on the chapters: true if it names a change to a tool.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-059,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would tying the first-hand observation to something I already do daily keep it going longer than the fixed time I chose?,"I choose times; habits form around cues. Automaticity grew with a consistent cue and took a median of 66 days. Source: Lally 2010.",tie it to a daily routine from 5 October,keep the fixed time,news,70,72,80,68,80,explore,"Resolved by notes to 2026-10-31: true if each week has three observations.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-060,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would an afternoon walking a neighbourhood I have never been to, on Sunday 11 October, leave me in a better mood than a usual Sunday?","My days repeat the same rooms. Days with more varied places went with more positive mood. Source: Heller 2020.",do it on Sunday 11 October,keep Sunday as it is,news,68,70,92,66,70,explore,Resolved by a note dated by 2026-10-12 on the afternoon.,2026-10-12,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-061,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Has an experiment I ran since September changed a plan of mine more than any book or paper did?,"Candidate effective variable: small experiments beat more reading when the uncertainty is empirical. Source: my notes.",keep experiments first,give reading equal standing in the variable's note,synthesis,80,70,64,76,88,exploit,Resolved by a later note naming the experiment or the book; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-062,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would a crewmate's phone screenshots of each restyled page catch more than my own look on my phone?,"Checking each restyled page on a phone before deploy was endorsed. Source: session 5.",brief a crewmate for screenshots of each restyled page,look at them myself on my phone,calibration,72,74,66,76,84,exploit,Resolved by a later note comparing the two checks; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-063,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would a screen-free skill I practise ten minutes a day, such as juggling three balls, be a better break between mathematics problems than checking the fleet?","My breaks are screens. Three months of juggling practice changed brain grey matter in adults. Source: Draganski 2004.",get three balls and start on 5 October,keep breaks as they are,news,66,66,94,66,68,explore,Resolved by a later note on the breaks; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-064,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would writing three things that went well, and why, each night from 5 to 11 October lift my mood more than my usual notes do?","My notes record problems and plans. This exercise raised happiness for six months in a randomised trial. Source: Seligman 2005.",do it those seven nights,skip it,news,68,68,86,66,72,explore,Resolved by a later note on the week; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-065,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Should Calibrator keep its WebMCP tools when they come out of the other visualisations?,"Its five read-only tools let an agent read the session and validate a TOON before I paste it. Source: calibrator SKILLS.md.",keep Calibrator's tools and remove the rest,"remove them from every visualisation, Calibrator included",project,70,66,72,70,86,exploit,"Resolved by the catalogue on 2026-10-31: true if calibrator.yaml still lists webmcp_tools while most others do not.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-066,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would doing one mathematics block a week somewhere other than my desk, such as a library, help me remember more of what I study?","All my study happens in one place. Studying the same material in two rooms improved recall over one room. Source: Smith 1978.",hold one block in a library in the week of 5 October,keep every block at the desk,news,66,68,84,62,78,explore,Resolved by a later note on the library block; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-067,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would I drop the mental-computation ladder check due 31 October to make room for a strength-morning todo?,"The ladder check is one of my eight; the strength mornings are not. Source: my notes, 2 October.",swap them tonight,keep the ladder check,notes,70,78,62,74,84,exploit,"Resolved by a later note on the todo list: true if the swap is recorded.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-068,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would a dimensional-analysis check of my QED-to-epidemics post find an error in it?,"Physics needs two cards a session; that post is my one public physics argument. Source: my notes, 2 October.",have a crewmate check it by 16 October,leave the post as it is,synthesis,70,62,76,72,78,explore,"Resolved by a note recording the check: true if it finds an error.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-069,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would a fixed monthly transfer to savings, set up by 16 October, still be running untouched in a year?","Money is a domain my notes skip. Automatic escalation raised savings rates from 3.5% to 13.6% in 40 months. Source: Thaler 2004.",set it up by 16 October,leave money as it is,news,66,70,88,64,66,explore,Resolved by a note in October 2027; unresolved otherwise.,2027-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-070,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would no caffeine after 14:00 in the week from 5 October give me more sleep than that week with my usual intake?","Never on my list. 400 mg of caffeine six hours before bed cut sleep by over an hour. If I take none, this is near 0. Source: Drake 2013.","take no caffeine after 14:00 from 5 October",leave caffeine as it is,news,66,70,84,62,72,explore,Resolved by a later note on that week's sleep; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-071,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will the first live defect recorded in October be found by me rather than by an automated check?,"Re-asked with reworded actions; 16 of 20 resolved answers at 70 or more came true. Source: session 5.",look at five live pages myself each Sunday,brief the per-deploy browser check by 9 October,calibration,78,76,54,76,86,exploit,"Resolved by the first note recording a live defect in October: true if I found it.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-072,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would I swap editing the Calibrator post for posting the beamdiag question in my eight todos?,"My todo list holds eight and is full; the post went live as a draft for me to edit. Source: my notes, 2 October.",swap them tonight,keep the post edit in the eight,notes,72,80,58,70,86,exploit,"Resolved by a later note on the todo list: true if the swap is recorded.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-073,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Do I trust automated checks mainly because reviewing agents' work bores me?,"Re-asked with reworded actions, since the wording of such actions may sway me. Source: session 5.",read one landed diff for 20 minutes each Friday,leave review to CI and the checks,calibration,76,74,52,84,86,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note gives the reason; then resolved by that note.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-074,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will my first fleet-free evening happen in the week starting 5 October?,"Firstmate holds all decisions that evening; no evening is named. Source: session 5.",keep it as a note,name the evening tonight,calibration,70,78,56,76,86,exploit,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-11 recording a fleet-free evening: true if one happened.",2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-075,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will I write the first weekly status line myself by Sunday 4 October?,"The status line lives in my notes under a status tag. Source: session 5.",write it on Sunday,have a crewmate draft it for me to edit,calibration,70,72,60,76,84,exploit,Resolved true if a note tagged status dated by 2026-10-04 is not #agent-written; false otherwise.,2026-10-04,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-076,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Should December's quantum field theory start from the renormalisation group rather than from scattering amplitudes?,"The one-loop QED beta function I plan to redo is a renormalisation-group result. Source: my notes, 2 October.",start December from the renormalisation group,start from scattering amplitudes,notes,68,66,78,60,80,explore,"Resolved by December's first physics note: true if it starts from the renormalisation group.",2026-12-15,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-077,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would spending about 20 dollars on someone else by 10 October lift my mood more than spending it on myself?,"My spending decisions are about the fleet. Money spent on others raised happiness more than money spent on oneself. Source: Dunn 2008.",do it by 10 October,skip it,news,64,66,90,64,64,explore,Resolved by a later note recording it; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-078,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Should the eccentric bolt-group extension of fastener-cg be checked against Brandt's 1982 worked examples before it ships?,"fastener-cg already compares an instantaneous-centre solve with the elastic method. Source: AISC Engineering Journal, 1982.",make Brandt's two examples its acceptance test,rely on its own tests,project,70,72,68,62,82,exploit,"Resolved by the fastener-cg repository on 2026-10-31: true if a test reproduces Brandt's examples.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-079,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"A month after giving 1% of October's agent spend to a GiveWell top charity, by 31 October, would I still endorse it?","My money decisions are about the fleet. GiveWell lists charities it finds most cost-effective. Source: GiveWell.",give it by 31 October,skip it,news,62,64,90,66,62,explore,Resolved by a note in November on the gift; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-080,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will the next note dated after tonight be a first-hand mathematics or engineering note I wrote myself?,"A hiring manager reading this week's notes would see mostly agent management. Source: session 5.",keep the order as it is,write a short one tomorrow before any agent note,calibration,66,72,58,78,84,exploit,"Resolved by the first note dated 2026-10-03 or later: true if it is first-hand mathematics or engineering without #agent-written.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-081,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"With 80 as the endorsement threshold, should answers of 20 or less endorse the low action?","Of 20 resolved answers at 70 or more, 16 came true; of 8 at 30 or less, 6 came false. Source: raw.toon.",use 20 for the low action,keep 30 for the low action,calibration,74,68,62,64,86,exploit,"Resolved by the next reading-rule note: true if it sets 20 for the low action.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-082,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would a weekly 15-minute walk spent looking for something that amazes me, from 5 October, lift my mood more than a walk with a podcast?","My walks, if any, are for getting somewhere. Weekly awe walks raised joy and prosocial feeling over eight weeks. Source: Sturm 2022.",take the first on 5 October,skip it,news,62,64,90,62,64,explore,Resolved by a later note on the walks; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-083,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Should the site's own pages, notes and blog take the style guide before any new visualisation is built?","Over 30 restyles have landed on the site, the latest four batches today. Source: site PRs 139 to 142.",restyle the site's pages next,let new visualisations go first,project,66,70,64,68,82,exploit,"Resolved by the site on 2026-10-31: true if the site's pages were restyled before any new visualisation landed.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-084,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would moving the gym-bag outcome and the Open questions prune to 16 October tonight make the other 9 and 10 October deadlines likelier to be met?,"Five todos fall on 9 and 10 October. Source: my notes, 2 October.",move those two to 16 October tonight,keep every date,notes,68,76,56,72,84,exploit,"Resolved by notes after 2026-10-10: true if the other deadlines on those days were all met.",2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-085,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Should a crewmate start the fastener-cg extension before 9 October, now that the restyle ports have landed?","The sweep was to finish first; its site ports landed today. Source: site PRs 139 to 142.","brief it tomorrow, 3 October",wait until the site's own pages are restyled,project,68,76,58,66,84,exploit,"Resolved by the fastener-cg repository: true if work on the extension starts before 2026-10-09.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-086,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Should the deploy lock be a file the deploy step checks, rather than a rule in every brief?","Today each brief tells a crewmate to check other lanes before deploying; the playbook has no lock. Source: site deploy playbook.",brief a crewmate to add the lock to the deploy step by 16 October,keep the rule in each brief,project,66,74,62,66,80,exploit,"Resolved by the deploy playbook on 2026-10-31: true if it checks a lock file; false otherwise.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-087,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would I answer all of a 150-card session 7 within a day of receiving it?,"Session 5 asked whether 150 cards would give me more than 100; this asks whether I would finish them. Source: session 5.",generate 150 cards for session 7,keep 100,calibration,72,70,56,66,86,exploit,"Resolved by session 7's export if it has 150 cards: true if all were answered within a day.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-088,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Would my own three-sentence reading of the Kun Chen interview, written tonight, differ from the agent's?","The interview's psychoanalytic note is agent-written; I was unsure I agree with it. Source: my notes, 2 October.",write mine tonight,leave the agent's note as it is,notes,66,60,66,70,76,explore,"Resolved by a later note with my reading: true if it differs in substance.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-089,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Am I answering Calibrator to feel decisive more than to change what I do?,"Six of session 3's nine dated-todo cards stayed notes. Source: my notes, 2 October.",start each session with cards on what I did since the last,keep sessions forward-looking only,calibration,80,72,40,84,90,exploit,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-16 counting session-3 actions taken: true if fewer than three were done.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-090,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would I listen to the Calibrator podcast episode if it reached my phone's podcast app instead of the site?,"It is only on the site, and no new episode is made until I have heard one. Source: site PR 130.",ask a crewmate for a podcast feed,keep episodes on the site,project,66,66,66,62,76,explore,"Resolved by a later note: true if I listen in full after a feed exists.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-091,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Should the cap on new repositories for October be written into firstmate's brief template?,"My public repositories number 61; the cap stands on one Calibrator answer. Source: GitHub.",add it to the template by 5 October,leave it to my answers,project,64,70,60,66,80,exploit,"Resolved by firstmate's brief template on 2026-10-31: true if it states the cap.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-092,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Should firstmate's standing rules, such as never writing to Downloads, Desktop or Documents, be enforced by a hook rather than in briefs?","Those rules are new and live only in crewmate briefs; the curfew already goes to a hook. Source: my notes, 2 October.",brief a hook that blocks those writes by 16 October,keep them in briefs,project,64,68,64,62,78,explore,"Resolved by a later note: true if a hook enforces them by 2026-10-31.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-093,cal-2026-10-02-s6,"Will my next export arrive without garbled characters, as session 5's did?","Session 5's export matched the published session exactly; earlier ones needed accents restored. Source: session 5.",drop the paste-path test,brief the paste-path test as endorsed,calibration,64,60,66,58,80,exploit,"Resolved by session 6's recording: true if its export needs no restoration.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-094,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Will I watch the Kun Chen deck through once by 9 October?,"It went live today as a narrated deck. Source: site PR 137.",keep making a deck for each interview I note,make no more interview decks until I have watched one,project,62,66,58,64,76,exploit,"Resolved by a later note: true if it records watching the deck through by 2026-10-09.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-095,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Did agent work crowd out time with people this week?,"A September note separates withdrawing from others from evidence about them. Source: my notes.",keep one evening a week free of the fleet,keep evenings open,notes,70,72,40,76,86,exploit,Resolved by my answer as a fact about this week; a later note may record the evening.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-096,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would my Gameweek 6 wildcard squad differ by more than two players from the one I would pick tonight?,"I pick the squad myself between 7 and 10 October. Source: my notes, 2 October.",wait until 7 October as planned,pick it tonight and stop thinking about it,notes,62,70,56,60,72,exploit,"Resolved by a note on the wildcard comparing the final squad with tonight's: true if more than two differ.",2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-097,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Would explaining one étale-cohomology result to a person beat writing a note on it?,Every mathematics note I write is for myself.,find one listener in November,keep writing notes,synthesis,72,70,40,70,84,exploit,Resolved by a November note comparing the two; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-098,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Is Calibrator the most useful thing I built this month?,"Three sessions, 305 answered cards and 26 notes on 2 October. Source: raw.toon.",point the next tooling effort at Calibrator,point it elsewhere,synthesis,70,68,40,66,86,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note ranks this month's builds; then resolved by it.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-099,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Did I enjoy most of this week's work?,"This week was mostly agent tooling and site work. Source: my notes.",keep the week's mix,cut first the part I did not enjoy,notes,66,64,40,62,84,exploit,Resolved by my answer as a fact about this week.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s6-100,cal-2026-10-02-s6,Could I find the speaker of “I would rather lose than sell out” in ten minutes tonight?,"Its todo is on the Open questions page, which I prune by 9 October. Source: my notes.",search for ten minutes tonight,drop it in the prune,notes,56,60,54,50,66,exploit,Resolved by a later note naming the speaker or dropping the item.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T10:45:00Z"
sources[105]{question_id,source_id,title,url,published_at,retrieved_at}:
